IMPORT prelude

-- Independence of Singapore Agreement 1965 (Singapore) -- what separation from Malaysia decided for people, property and
-- agreements: the date (Article II and Annex B s 3), the end of the Malaysian constitution in Singapore (Annex B s 3), the
-- head of state (s 6), the continuation of existing laws (s 7), the courts and appeals (s 8), property and liabilities
-- (s 9), public officers (s 10), Singapore's members of the Malaysian Parliament (s 11), citizenship (s 12), treaties and
-- decisions of international organisations (s 13), the Johore Water Agreements (s 14), the rescission of Annexes J and K of
-- the 1963 Malaysia Agreement (Article VII), and Singapore's indemnity for guarantees given by Malaysia (Article VIII).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/ISA1965.txt and ISA1965.pdf. The cover page says
-- "This revised edition incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on
-- 31 December 2021". No amendment is annotated anywhere in the deposit. THE .txt DEPOSIT HOLDS ONLY THAT COVER PAGE: the
-- instrument itself is in the .pdf as sixteen scanned facsimile pages with no text layer, and was read from page images.
-- The facsimile reproduces, in order: Singapore's Proclamation of Singapore (9 August 1965, signed by Lee Kuan Yew); the
-- Malaysian Proclamation on Singapore (9 August 1965, Tunku Abdul Rahman); the Agreement itself (Articles I-VIII, dated 7
-- August 1965, signed for both Governments); Annex A (the form of the Malaysian proclamation); and Annex B, "A Bill intituled
-- An Act to amend the Constitution of Malaysia and the Malaysia Act" (ss 1-14). The section numbers below are Annex B's.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0257 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Agreement decides for a person or business it applies to; no
-- scenario has asked a sharper question yet. SCOPED to the provisions that decide something about a person, an officer, a
-- piece of property, a law or an agreement. Not encoded: the recitals and proclamations except as quoted, Article III (the
-- form of proclamation), Article IV (Malaysia's undertaking to enact Annex B), Article V (the promised defence treaty and its
-- joint defence council, bases and the no-detrimental-treaty undertaking), Article VI (economic co-operation), Annex B ss 2,
-- 4 and 5 (the powers provisions), and the second paragraph of s 13 (the 1957 UK-Malaya defence agreement and the British
-- bases).
--
-- Dates are written as numbers YYYYMMDD (9 August 1965 is 19650809), so that ordinary number comparison orders them.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Independence of Singapore Agreement 1965 -- separation`

§§ `Article II and Annex B s 3 -- Singapore Day`

-- Article II: "Singapore shall cease to be a State of Malaysia on the 9th day of August, 1965, (hereinafter referred to as
-- "Singapore Day") and shall become an independent and sovereign state separate from and independent of Malaysia".
-- Annex B s 3 repeats this and adds: "accordingly the Constitution of Malaysia and the Malaysia Act shall thereupon cease to
-- have effect in Singapore except as hereinafter provided."
-- Recitals: "Malaysia was established on the 16th day of September, 1963". Annex B ss 9 and 10 use "Malaysia Day" without
-- defining it; reading it as 16 September 1963 is an INFERENCE from the recital.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Singapore Day` MEANS 19650809

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Malaysia Day` MEANS 19630916

GIVEN `the date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Singapore is a State of Malaysia on` IF
        `the date` AT LEAST `Malaysia Day`
    AND `the date` LESS THAN `Singapore Day`

-- "except as hereinafter provided": s 8 keeps the Malaysian appeal route for the time being (below).
GIVEN `the date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Constitution of Malaysia has effect in Singapore on` IF
    `Singapore is a State of Malaysia on` `the date`

§§ `Annex B s 6 -- the head of state`

-- s 6: "The Yang di-Pertuan Agong shall on Singapore Day cease to be the Supreme Head of Singapore and his sovereignty and
-- jurisdiction, and power and authority, executive or otherwise in respect of Singapore shall be relinquished and shall vest
-- in the Yang di-Pertuan Negara, the Head of State of Singapore."
-- The deposit says nothing about who held that position before Malaysia Day.
DECLARE Sovereign IS ONE OF
    `the Yang di-Pertuan Agong`
    `the Yang di-Pertuan Negara`
    `not stated in the deposit`

GIVEN `the date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Sovereign
`sovereignty over Singapore rests with` MEANS
    IF `the date` AT LEAST `Singapore Day` THEN `the Yang di-Pertuan Negara`
    ELSE IF `the date` AT LEAST `Malaysia Day` THEN `the Yang di-Pertuan Agong`
         ELSE `not stated in the deposit`

§§ `Annex B s 7 -- existing laws continue`

-- s 7: "All present laws in force in Singapore immediately before Singapore Day shall continue to have effect according to
-- their tenor and shall be construed as if this Act had not been passed in respect of Singapore subject however to amendment
-- or repeal by the Legislature of Singapore."
GIVEN `in force in Singapore immediately before Singapore Day` IS A BOOLEAN, `amended or repealed by the Legislature of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the law continues unchanged by s 7` IF
    `in force in Singapore immediately before Singapore Day` AND (NOT `amended or repealed by the Legislature of Singapore`)

§§ `Annex B s 8 -- courts and appeals`

-- s 8: "Until other provision is made by the Legislature of Singapore, the jurisdiction, original or appellate, and the
-- practice and procedure of the High Court and the subordinate Courts of Singapore shall be the same as that exercised and
-- followed immediately before Singapore Day, and appeals from the High Court shall continue to lie to the Federal Court of
-- Appeal of Malaysia and then to the Privy Council in like manner."
-- Whether and when the Legislature of Singapore made other provision is not in the deposit.
DECLARE AppealRoute IS ONE OF
    `the Federal Court of Appeal of Malaysia, then the Privy Council`
    `as the Legislature of Singapore provides`

GIVEN `the Legislature of Singapore has made other provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN AppealRoute
`an appeal from the Singapore High Court lies to` MEANS
    IF `the Legislature of Singapore has made other provision`
    THEN `as the Legislature of Singapore provides`
    ELSE `the Federal Court of Appeal of Malaysia, then the Privy Council`

§§ `Annex B s 9 -- property, rights and liabilities`

-- s 9: "All property, movable and immovable, and rights, liabilities and obligations which before Malaysia Day belonged to or
-- were the responsibility of the Government of Singapore and which on that day or after became the property of or the
-- responsibility of the Government of Malaysia shall on Singapore Day revert to and vest in or devolve upon and become once
-- again the property of or the responsibility of Singapore."
-- Property Malaysia acquired for itself in Singapore between the two days is not caught by s 9 (the text is silent on it).
GIVEN `belonged to the Government of Singapore before Malaysia Day` IS A BOOLEAN, `passed to the Government of Malaysia on or after Malaysia Day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it reverts to Singapore under s 9` IF
    `belonged to the Government of Singapore before Malaysia Day` AND `passed to the Government of Malaysia on or after Malaysia Day`

§§ `Annex B s 10 -- public officers`

-- s 10(a): "All persons, including members of the Armed Forces, the Police Force, the Courts and the Judiciary, and all others
-- who immediately before Malaysia Day were officers employed by the Government of Singapore and who on that day or after
-- became officers employed by the Government of Malaysia shall on Singapore Day become once again officers employed by the
-- Government of Singapore."
-- (b): "All persons who between Malaysia Day and Singapore Day were engaged by the Government of Malaysia for employment in
-- those departments which were departments of the State of Singapore before Malaysia Day shall on Singapore Day become
-- forthwith officers employed by the Government of Singapore."
DECLARE Officer HAS
    `a Singapore government officer immediately before Malaysia Day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `became a Malaysian government officer on or after Malaysia Day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `engaged by Malaysia between Malaysia Day and Singapore Day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in a department that was a Singapore State department before Malaysia Day` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the officer` IS AN Officer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `becomes a Singapore government officer on Singapore Day` IF
        (    `the officer`'s `a Singapore government officer immediately before Malaysia Day`
         AND `the officer`'s `became a Malaysian government officer on or after Malaysia Day`)
    OR  (    `the officer`'s `engaged by Malaysia between Malaysia Day and Singapore Day`
         AND `the officer`'s `in a department that was a Singapore State department before Malaysia Day`)

§§ `Annex B s 11 -- Singapore's members of the Malaysian Parliament`

-- s 11: "The two Senators and fifteen Members of Parliament from Singapore shall on Singapore Day cease to be members of the
-- Senate and the House of Representatives respectively."
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Singapore seats vacated on Singapore Day` MEANS 2 PLUS 15

GIVEN `sits for Singapore in the Malaysian Senate or House` IS A BOOLEAN, `the date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `still a member of the Malaysian Parliament for Singapore` IF
    `sits for Singapore in the Malaysian Senate or House` AND `the date` LESS THAN `Singapore Day`

§§ `Annex B s 12 -- citizenship`

-- s 12: "A citizen of Singapore shall on Singapore Day cease to be a citizen of Malaysia."
-- s 12 says nothing about anyone who is not a citizen of Singapore; this rule only says whether s 12 takes Malaysian
-- citizenship away.
GIVEN `a citizen of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `the date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 12 has ended Malaysian citizenship` IF
    `a citizen of Singapore` AND `the date` AT LEAST `Singapore Day`

§§ `Annex B s 13 -- treaties and decisions of international organisations`

-- s 13: "Any treaty, agreement or convention entered into before Singapore Day between the Yang di-Pertuan Agong or the
-- Government of Malaysia and another country or countries, including those deemed to be so by Article 169 of the
-- Constitution of Malaysia shall in so far as such instruments have application to Singapore, be deemed to be a treaty,
-- agreement or convention between Singapore and that country or countries, and any decision taken by an international
-- organisation and accepted before Singapore Day by the Government of Malaysia shall in so far as that decision has
-- application to Singapore be deemed to be a decision of an international organisation of which Singapore is a member."
GIVEN `entered into on` IS A NUMBER, `made by the Agong or the Government of Malaysia with another country` IS A BOOLEAN, `has application to Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the treaty binds Singapore and that country under s 13` IF
        `entered into on` LESS THAN `Singapore Day`
    AND `made by the Agong or the Government of Malaysia with another country`
    AND `has application to Singapore`

GIVEN `accepted by Malaysia on` IS A NUMBER, `has application to Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision is deemed one of an organisation Singapore belongs to` IF
    `accepted by Malaysia on` LESS THAN `Singapore Day` AND `has application to Singapore`

§§ `Annex B s 14 -- the Water Agreements`

-- s 14: "The Government of Singapore shall guarantee that the Public Utilities Board of Singapore shall on and after Singapore
-- Day abide by the terms and conditions of the Water Agreements dated 1st September, 1961, and 29th September, 1962, entered
-- into between the City Council of Singapore and the Government of the State of Johore. The Government of Malaysia shall
-- guarantee that the Government of the State of Johore will on and after Singapore Day also abide by the terms and conditions
-- of the said two Water Agreements."
GIVEN `dated` IS A NUMBER, `between the City Council of Singapore and Johore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a Water Agreement guaranteed by s 14` IF
    (`dated` EQUALS 19610901 OR `dated` EQUALS 19620929) AND `between the City Council of Singapore and Johore`

DECLARE Guarantor IS ONE OF
    `the Government of Singapore`
    `the Government of Malaysia`
    `nobody under s 14`

DECLARE WaterParty IS ONE OF
    `the Public Utilities Board`
    `the Government of the State of Johore`
    `another body`

GIVEN `the party` IS A WaterParty
GIVETH A Guarantor
`who guarantees that party's performance` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the party`
    WHEN `the Public Utilities Board` THEN `the Government of Singapore`
    WHEN `the Government of the State of Johore` THEN `the Government of Malaysia`
    OTHERWISE `nobody under s 14`

§§ `Article VII -- Annexes J and K of the 1963 Agreement rescinded`

-- Article VII: "The provisions of Annex J and K of the Agreement relating to Malaysia dated the 9th day of July, 1963 are hereby
-- expressly rescinded as from the date of this Agreement." The Agreement is dated 7 August 1965 -- two days BEFORE Singapore
-- Day. What Annexes J and K contained is not in the deposit.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the date of this Agreement` MEANS 19650807

GIVEN `the date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Annexes J and K are still operative on` IF
    `the date` LESS THAN `the date of this Agreement`

§§ `Article VIII -- guarantees given by Malaysia`

-- Article VIII: "With regard to any agreement entered into between the Government of Singapore and any other country or
-- corporate body which has been guaranteed by the Government of Malaysia, the Government of Singapore hereby undertakes to
-- negotiate with such country or corporate body to enter into a fresh agreement releasing the Government of Malaysia of its
-- liabilities and obligations under the said guarantee, and the Government of Singapore hereby undertakes to indemnify the
-- Government of Malaysia fully for any liabilities, obligations or damage which it may suffer as a result of the said
-- guarantee."
GIVEN `a Singapore Government agreement with a country or corporate body` IS A BOOLEAN, `guaranteed by the Government of Malaysia` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Singapore must negotiate a release of Malaysia` IF
    `a Singapore Government agreement with a country or corporate body` AND `guaranteed by the Government of Malaysia`

-- "fully": the indemnity equals the whole loss; no cap or share is stated.
GIVEN `guaranteed agreement` IS A BOOLEAN, `Malaysia's loss under the guarantee` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Singapore's indemnity to Malaysia` MEANS
    IF `guaranteed agreement` THEN `Malaysia's loss under the guarantee` ELSE 0
